                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On January 29, 1954, Senator John C.
                        Stennis of Mississippi, member of the Senate Committee on Armed
                    Services, transmitted a letter to Charles E.
                        Wilson, Secretary of Defense, expressing opposition to
                    participation by the United States in the war in Indochina. For text, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">United States-Vietnam Relations, 1945–1967</hi>, Book 9,
                    page 239.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
